<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle active at $112/dressed - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle active at $112/dressed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading on slaughter steers and heifers was very active, USDA said. Compared to last Thursday live sales $1.00-$2.00 per cwt higher; dressed basis $2.00-$3.00 higher. Demand and seller interest excellent.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered ( paid on hot carcass weights).</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers - Select and Choice 2-3 1200-1325 lbs -</p>
<p>69.00-70.00; dressed basis mostly 112.00, instances early to</p>
<p>110.00. Slaughter heifers - Select and Choice 2-3 1050-1225</p>
<p>lbs - 69.00-70.00; dressed basis 111.00-112.00, latest trades</p>
<p>mostly 112.00.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed - 10,000   For the week - 15,000</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
